\item a genus in \code{keep} or \code{drop} (\code{"Populus"}) matches every species of that
genus in the key, and a species (\code{"Populus balsamifera"}) matches its
subspecies and varieties (\code{"Populus balsamifera subsp. trichocarpa"});
\item a name matches the same name followed by its author
(\code{"Quercus macrocarpa"} and \code{"Quercus macrocarpa Michx."}, or
\code{"Carcharodon carcharias (Linnaeus, 1758)"}), whichever of the two has
the author;
\item a species in \code{keep} (\code{"Quercus macrocarpa"}) keeps a result of the key
that is only its genus (\code{"Quercus"}), and a subspecies keeps its
species. This is not done for \code{drop}: removing one species does not
